@startuml records-flow-cli
title The structured output directory: the CLI's path to it

skinparam defaultFontSize 12

actor User
participant "bertini2 (CLI)" as CLI
participant "ZeroDim solver\n(the emission seam)" as Solver
database "output directory\n(default: ./bertini_output)" as Dir

User -> CLI : bertini2 input
note right of CLI
  records are ordinary output, like main_data:
  produced always, freely deletable, no flag.
  BERTINI_RECORDS_DIR relocates them;
  BERTINI_RECORDS_DIR="" is the OFF switch.
  Manager rank only under MPI
  (mpirun -x BERTINI_RECORDS_DIR).
end note
CLI -> Dir : archive the input file\n(kind="given", role=cli_input)
CLI -> Solver : solve

group ensure-answered
  Solver -> Dir : scan history for this ask\n(target digest + homotopy digest\n+ FULL settings digest + seed)
  Dir --> Solver : recorded paths
  Solver -> Solver : HYDRATE recorded paths,\ncompute only the missing\n(a killed run FINISHES on rerun)
end

Solver -> Dir : run header (kind="run"):\nask, producer{name,version,commit},\nvariables + variables_user, num_paths
Solver -> Dir : definitions/ (content-addressed):\ntarget rendering, config JSON
loop every tracked path
  Solver -> Dir : track record: status\n(success | diverged | failed),\nSuccessCode name + integers,\nendpoint + endpoint_user,\nfunction_residual, start provenance
end
Solver -> Dir : auto-declare finite solutions\n(kind="result")
Solver -> Dir : render results.json + INDEX.txt

note over Dir
  **the directory, readable with NO software:**
  README.txt      what this is (self-documenting)
  results.json    declared results, pretty, SELF-COMPLETE
                  (results first, then refs to the system,
                  configs, seed that produced them)
  INDEX.txt       one line per run
  history/        JSONL journals, one writer per file
  definitions/    content-addressed (sha256sum verifies)
end note

User -> Dir : eyes / grep / jq / pandas / sha256sum
@enduml
